tasks.description:
Create `src/types.ts` with TypeScript interfaces for Ralph's core data structures. Port these from the shapes used in the shell/Python code.

**RalphConfig** — matches ralph.json shape:
```ts
interface RalphConfig {
  projectName: string;
  projectDescription: string;
  healthCheck: string;
  defaultTestCommand: string;
  implementationFile: string;
  truncateText: boolean;
  summarize: { claudeMdPattern: string };
  narration: {
    enabled: boolean;
    voice: string;
    ntfyTopic: string;
  };
}
```

**Task** — matches tasks.json task shape (see `lib/tasks.schema.json` for the authoritative schema):
```ts
interface Task {
  id: number;
  priority: number;
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  directory?: string;
  status: 'pending' | 'in-progress' | 'complete' | 'blocked';
  files?: string[];
  tests?: string[];
  completedAt?: string;
  completedBy?: string;
  notes?: string;
  dependencies?: number[];
  model?: 'opus' | 'sonnet';
  agent?: string;
}
```

**AgentInfo** — matches the shape from `_ralph_discover_agents()` in `lib/ralph_config.sh`:
```ts
interface AgentInfo {
  name: string;
  description: string;
  model: string;
  file: string;
}
```

Export all interfaces. Also export type guard functions (`isValidConfig`, `isValidTask`) that validate unknown data against the expected shapes. These should check required fields exist and have correct types.

Write tests in `test/types.test.ts` that verify the type guards accept valid data and reject malformed data (missing fields, wrong types).

Create src/test-validator.ts and test/test-validator.test.ts. Port the post-iteration test validation from ralph_execute.sh (lines 551-627).

Implement:
- validateTaskTests(opts: { task: Task, tasksFilePath: string, projectRoot: string }): Promise<{ status: 'passed' | 'failed' | 'error' | 'skipped', message?: string }>

Behavior:
- Read task meta to get test commands from task.tests array
- If no tests defined, return { status: 'skipped' }
- Check if the task was marked complete in tasks.json (re-read file to get current status)
- Run each test command from the task's resolved directory (projectRoot + task.directory) with a 120s timeout
- Smart failure detection: distinguish 'can't run' (missing script, MODULE_NOT_FOUND, command not found → exit code 127) from 'ran but failed' (non-zero exit with test output)
- On real test failure: revert task status to 'in-progress' in tasks.json, append failure note to task.notes, return { status: 'failed', message }
- On infrastructure error (can't run): append note but DON'T revert status, return { status: 'error', message }
- On all tests passing: return { status: 'passed' }

Make the file I/O (reading/writing tasks.json) injectable or use the filesystem directly as the shell version does.
